# Check every text file out with LF, whatever a contributor's core.autocrlf is
# set to. Git for Windows defaults it to true, which would otherwise give a
# Windows clone CRLF working files and fail tests/docs.rs, since that test
# compares generated LF text against the bytes of docs/rules.md.
#
# The CRLF fixtures the line-endings rule is tested with are Rust string
# literals rather than files on disk, so nothing here needs an exception. A
# fixture that has to keep its CRLF on disk would need one.
* text=auto eol=lf

